# Build output.
#
# The leading slash on these ANCHORS them to the repository root. Without
# it, `build/` matches a directory called `build` at any depth - which
# silently swallowed `.github/actions/build/`, so the composite action
# both workflows call was never committed and every CI run died with
# "Can't find 'action.yml'". Nothing showed in `git status`, because
# ignored files do not.
#
# relbuild/ and debbuild/ stay unanchored on purpose: each plugin writes
# its own, under plugins/<name>/.
/build/
relbuild/
debbuild/
/dist/
/x64/
/Debug/
/Release/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
!lib/libMinHook.*.lib

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.VC.db
